VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'virtual chair is where he can sit but still having&nbsp; the reference of the virtual world. Yes. Exactly.&nbsp;&nbsp; So what are what is actually tracked right?&nbsp; Because of course with a headset you can track&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[05:18] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the head. What about the rest of the body of the&nbsp; performance? Yeah. So um with the headset we track&nbsp;&nbsp; uh the eye tracking, the facial tracking if you\'re&nbsp; working with the Quest Pro. Uh we then also track&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[05:32] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'the position of the headset and controllers.&nbsp; um which we initially did. So we want to have&nbsp;&nbsp; this as a tool that can work in your bedroom, in&nbsp; the classroom and in a studio environment. Um so&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[05:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'we are access uh we work with a lot of different&nbsp; motion capture solutions. Um so initially we did&nbsp;&nbsp; inverse kinematics IK which uh always looked a bit&nbsp; ropey for the base version. Um, so what we did was&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[06:05] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'we trained our own AI solution based off um, just&nbsp; the positions and rotations of the headsets and&nbsp;&nbsp; controllers to basically allow you to extrapolate&nbsp; from that as to what the full body is doing. So,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[06:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'uh, it\'s not perfect for dancing, but for all your&nbsp; kind of locomotion stuff, uh, it looks a lot more&nbsp;&nbsp; natural than inverse kinematics. Um, then we\'re&nbsp; also compatible with uh Xense motion capture suits&nbsp;&nbsp; and uh Vicon. Um, so you can really work your way&nbsp; up the different uh motion capture qualities. Um,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[06:39] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'but what we\'ve kind of insisted on the whole&nbsp; way along is that we\'re working with uh properly&nbsp;&nbsp; real-time technologies. So, uh, if things aren\'t&nbsp; quite real time, then what happens is you reach&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[06:53] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'out to grab a pop a prop and there\'s a delay. You&nbsp; do that and then there\'s a second delay which a&nbsp;&nbsp; lot of the video solutions uh have that delay in&nbsp; them. Uh, and that doesn\'t work for uh embodied&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[07:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'performance which is uh the key thing we\'re trying&nbsp; to do. So you said another important thing and&nbsp;&nbsp; being like video AI solution something that we are&nbsp; going to we are going to also tackle and discuss&nbsp;&nbsp;'

