[07:50] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'so we captured around 15 hours of uh highquality&nbsp; Vicon motion captured data. Um so this essentially&nbsp;&nbsp; looks like uh a bunch of performers having to&nbsp; walk slow, walk medium, walk fast. um change&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[08:07] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'direction lots um to create a huge data set. Um&nbsp; so then what we\'re able to do is uh you know we&nbsp;&nbsp; don\'t actually also have to capture a data set&nbsp; of the three points in space. We can uh simulate&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[08:29] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'those points based off the uh track skeleton. Um&nbsp; but what this essentially means is we can make&nbsp;&nbsp; uh very natural uh movements and assumptions of&nbsp; what the legs are doing uh where the head is in&nbsp;&nbsp;'

