AUDIO: 'big is enough for your data set. Um [laughter] and&nbsp; uh it really depends on the research project um&nbsp;&nbsp; that you\'re trying to do. Um, so you know, as a as&nbsp; a frame of reference, I think the best thing you&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[10:21] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'can do is look for somebody who\'s done something&nbsp; close, uh, and work with similar volumes of data,&nbsp;&nbsp; uh, is typically the approach. I mean, uh,&nbsp; if you\'ve got the budget and you can afford&nbsp;&nbsp;'

[10:38] [scene:talk]
VISUAL: 
AUDIO: 'like to just go crazy at the data and that\'s&nbsp; fine. But if you\'ve got to capture it yourself,&nbsp;&nbsp; you\'ve got to kind of work out how much is enough.&nbsp; That\'s exactly the point, right? It\'s not because,&nbsp;&nbsp; oh, we should all have massive amount of data.&nbsp; You want the right amount of data for the job,&nbsp;&nbsp;'

